From 01b4f556b921c298749288e198cc9969816a9f83 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 05:49:49 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] fill dl-consolidation: checkpoint 1 (Games layer: P, S, H)

Promote the generic probability, simulation and hopping lemmas of DL-30,
DL-32, DL-33 and DL-34 to the Games layer and delete the copies:
- Games/Probability (ProbComp): expect_sample_equiv, expect_sample_comm,
  expect_sample_unique, expect_sub (from ChallengeSim); expect_sample_update
  (BitwiseSim's general form) and expect_sample_coord (AdaptiveCPA's form,
  derived from it); abs_expect_sub_le (from PRFGame).
- Games/Simulate: simulate_eq_of_abs (AdaptiveCPA) and
  simulate_eq_of_abs_bounded (PRFGame).
- Games/Hopping (ProbComp): expect_simulate_congr, prob_bad_le,
  expect_sample_mem_le (PRFGame).
- Games/BitCodec: the castImpl family (castImpl, castImpl_eq, castImpl_self,
  simulate_castImpl_toCompOn, expect_simulate_castImpl_toCompOn) from
  AdaptiveCPA/Hybrid; BitCodec now imports Games.Probability (acyclic).
- ChallengeSim: expect_simulate_eager moves here from BitwiseCPA/Eager, beside
  chRun (no Games module can state it; escalation note in the report).
ChallengeSim.expect_sample_prod stays (not a restatement of
Bridge.expect_sample_pair). Uses re-pointed; sketches and module docstrings
name the new homes.
